This repository holds no model weights. The voice bridge fetches some on
first use, and builds some third-party code from source. Their terms
follow.

Parakeet-TDT-0.6B v2
  The speech model the voice bridge uses on a desktop (voice_engine:
  parakeet). Made by NVIDIA and published at
  https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2 under the Creative
  Commons Attribution 4.0 International license (CC-BY-4.0),
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.
  The voice bridge fetches the F16 GGUF conversion of NVIDIA's original
  .nemo file published at https://huggingface.co/cstr/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2-GGUF
  (byte for byte what CrispASR's converter makes from NVIDIA's file; see
  ruling VO-16 in clients/ADJUDICATIONS.md) and quantizes it to Q4_K on
  the user's box. That conversion and quantization change the number
  format of the weights and nothing else.

Moonshine
  The speech models of voice_engine: moonshine (tiny, small, medium
  streaming English), by Moonshine AI, MIT license,
  https://github.com/moonshine-ai/moonshine.

CrispASR and ggml
  clients/go/scripts/native.sh --parakeet builds parakeet-cli from five
  source files of CrispASR (https://github.com/CrispStrobe/CrispASR, MIT
  license) and the CPU backend of its ggml fork
  (https://github.com/CrispStrobe/ggml, MIT license, a fork of
  https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml). Their license files are installed
  beside the binaries, under share/licenses.

ONNX Runtime
  native.sh --moonshine links Microsoft's ONNX Runtime release (MIT
  license); its license and third-party notices are installed beside
  moonshine-cli, under share/licenses. native.sh --onnxruntime installs the
  same pinned 1.23.2 release for the SmolVLA executor (the mujoco build tag
  and Cargo feature; the shipped binaries do not link it), with its license
  and notices under share/licenses/onnxruntime.

SmolVLA
  The SmolVLA executor runs lerobot/smolvla_base
  (https://huggingface.co/lerobot/smolvla_base, Apache License 2.0),
  exported to ONNX by clients/vla_export.py, with the tokenizer of its
  backbone HuggingFaceTB/SmolVLM2-500M-Video-Instruct
  (https://huggingface.co/HuggingFaceTB/SmolVLM2-500M-Video-Instruct,
  Apache License 2.0). Neither the weights nor the graphs are in this
  repository; they are kept in the user's cache.

MuJoCo
  The physics library of the Go and Rust robotics executors (the mujoco
  build tag and Cargo feature; the shipped binaries do not link it).
  clients/go/scripts/native.sh --mujoco installs the official MuJoCo
  3.12.0 release, checked against its published SHA-256, and the builds
  with the mujoco tag or feature link its libmujoco.so dynamically.
  Apache License 2.0, https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.
  Copyright 2021 DeepMind Technologies Limited.
  https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco. Its LICENSE and
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES are installed with it, under share/licenses/mujoco.

NVIDIA CUDA wheels
  The optional extras [search], [lora] and [vla] install torch, and the
  torch wheels pull NVIDIA's CUDA libraries (nvidia-* and cuda-* wheels)
  under NVIDIA's proprietary licence, not an open source one. Each user
  may install them for their own use. No bundle, release archive or
  default install of openDaisugi includes them, and the dev and CI
  environments do not install those extras.
